hreshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State explicitly that the 3.14-stable and sweep-lower-bounds cells must leave REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS UNSET (they install fewer extras than the gate), since tests/_extra_guard.py turns importorskip skips into hard errors when it is set — the plan's 'tests self-skip' and '0 failures' premises depend on it.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.25,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tests/conftest.py:137-145 imports _extra_guard and calls _extra_guard.install(); comment: 'With REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1 (set by the CI pytest steps) those skips become hard errors instead.'","tests/_extra_guard.py:32 ENV_VAR = \"REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS\"; strict_importorskip RAISES instead of skipping when the module is absent.","_build-and-test.yml sets `REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS: \"1\"` on BOTH pytest steps (lines 645, 716) and installs `--extra dev --extra reviewbot --extra ui` (line 355) so fastapi/jinja2 are present; the sweep jobs install FEWER extras (3.14 cell: bare `uv sync --locked`; sweep-lower-bounds: `.[dev,agents]`).","The plan says each sweep job uses 'the already-trusted setup-uv ... pattern' but never mentions REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS; test_extra_coverage_guard.py's REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS assertion is scoped to _BAT_YML only, so nothing forces the sweep jobs' choice either way."],"finding":"The plan's premise that ui/reviewbot tests 'self-skip via importorskip(\"fastapi\")' — and the derived claims '~0 genuine failures on 3.14 + the lock' and 'the full unit tier passes' / 'sweep-lower-bounds proves the floors work' — hold only when REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS is UNSET, a condition the plan never states or guarantees.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0494c60a64c999ca","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context/Problem (disentangling experiment; '~16 a PATH artifact', '0 genuine failures') + Approach items 1 (sweep-interpreters 3.14 `uv sync --locked`) and 4 (sweep-lower-bounds `.[dev,agents]`)","norm_id":"n1717237e03a19952","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer mirrors the gate's `env: REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS: \"1\"` block into sweep-lower-bounds or the 3.14 cell (which install neither ui nor reviewbot) — the fastapi/jinja2/httpx/boto3-gated tests hard-error instead of self-skipping, so the '0 failures' / 'unit tier passes' AC fails on a correct interpreter."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to Approach items 1 and 4: 'These cells deliberately do NOT set REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS (unlike the gate), because they install fewer extras and rely on the ui/reviewbot/pricing suites self-skipping via importorskip; tests/_extra_guard.py converts those skips into hard errors when REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","vague/subjective terms present: properly"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the in-session proving method for the sweep jobs' actual execution (e.g. trigger each via `workflow_dispatch` on the branch and record the run URLs/green status), rather than relying solely on a pre-plan experiment.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6","F1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4167,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Every new job is gated if: github.event_name == schedule || workflow_dispatch'","AC: 'the full unit tier passes on 3.14 + the lock'","The jobs never run on Verified/PR CI, so their pass state is not evaluable via the closing PR's CI"],"finding":"The five sweep jobs are schedule/workflow_dispatch-only, so they do NOT run on the closing PR's CI; yet AC lines assert observable outcomes ('the full unit tier passes on 3.14 + the lock', 'the full macOS and lower-bound jobs are real signals') whose green status cannot be produced by the PR's own CI. The plan proves only the two contract tests green on this change and relies on a pre-plan experiment for the 3.14 result — leaving no in-session proving command for the jobs' actual execution.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd6b571f9d8042bd7","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (3.14 stable cell / full macOS / lower-bound lines) + Approach (all jobs gated schedule/dispatch)"